description:
Found while writing JMAP-hwdv.7 integration tests.

Per RFC 8620 §5.3:

> The id property MUST NOT be set in the Create object (an immutable
> server-set property). If the object presents an id property, the
> server MUST respond with a SetError of type 'invalidProperties'
> citing 'id' in the properties array.

handle_task_list_set and handle_task_set (crate-jmap-tasks-server/src/) do not enforce this. A create with id: 'client-id' is silently accepted and the client-supplied id is replaced by the server-assigned id without any error signal.

Reproduction (TaskList/set):
```rust
let args = json!({
    "accountId": "acc1",
    "create": {
        "c1": { "id": "client-id", "name": "Inbox" }
    }
});
let (resp, _) = handle_task_list_set(&backend, args).await.unwrap();
// Expected: resp.notCreated.c1.type == "invalidProperties" and properties[0] == "id"
// Actual:   resp.created.c1 has the server-assigned id (e.g. "tasklist1"),
//           the client's "client-id" is silently dropped, notCreated is null
```

Same bug shape for Task/set (verified by ignored test task_set_create_with_client_id_rejects).

Same pattern was previously fixed for calendars-server as JMAP-r3pg.6.

The corresponding ignored tests in crate-jmap-tasks-server/tests/tasks_tests.rs are task_list_set_create_with_client_id_rejects and task_set_create_with_client_id_rejects.
